  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Mulliganed a keepable 7-card hand with 4 lands, a turn-1 cantrip (Scroll of Avacyn), and two solid creatures. The hand curves out reasonably: Scroll turn 1, crack turn 2 for card draw, Basri's Acolyte turn 4, Bulwark Giant turn 6. While slightly slow, it has consistent mana and card flow.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to mulligan to 6 cards",
      "better_line": "Keep the 7-card hand. It has adequate lands, a cantrip to smooth draws, and a reasonable curve. Going to 6 risks a worse hand for marginal improvement.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 2,
      "player": "Gem3P Coach",
      "decision_index": 2,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Hand has 4 lands and only 2 real spells (4-drop and 6-drop). Bottoming Scroll of Avacyn removes the only cheap cantrip that could help dig for action in an extremely land-heavy, action-light hand. The hand will do nothing until turn 4 at the earliest.",
      "action_taken": "Bottomed Scroll of Avacyn, keeping Bulwark Giant",
      "better_line": "Bottom Bulwark Giant instead - it's a 6-mana card that just gains life and blocks. Keeping Scroll of Avacyn provides a cheap way to cantrip on turn 2 to find more relevant spells, which is critical in a hand this land-heavy.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 2,
      "player": "Gem3P Coach",
      "decision_index": 2,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Chose Black for Thriving Heath when the deck likely contains Blue cards (Littjara Kinseekers, Mirror Image, Watertrap Weaver are all referenced cards that pair with the WU archetype). The hand is all white, but Thriving Heath's color choice matters for future draws, and choosing Blue would provide access to the deck's likely second color.",
      "action_taken": "Chose Black for Thriving Heath's color",
      "better_line": "Choose Blue for Thriving Heath, as the deck almost certainly has Blue cards that need colored mana support.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 12,
      "player": "Gem3P Coach",
      "decision_index": 10,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Passed with 3 mana available and Heirloom Blade in hand, which costs exactly 3 generic mana. Deploying the equipment now would set up efficient future turns - next turn they could play a 4-drop creature and equip for 1 mana the turn after, or play a cheaper creature and equip immediately.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority with 3 untapped Islands, doing nothing.",
      "better_line": "Cast Heirloom Blade for 3 mana to deploy it early, enabling efficient equip plays on future turns.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 34,
      "player": "Gem3F Tinker",
      "decision_index": 29,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Declined to attack with Watertrap Weaver when the opponent's only potential blocker is Celestial Enforcer 2/3. Tinker has Chilling Trap in hand, and since Watertrap Weaver is a Wizard, Chilling Trap cantrips. If Coach blocks with Enforcer, Tinker casts Chilling Trap on Enforcer (making it -2/3), saves the Weaver, draws a card, and deals 2 damage to the Enforcer. If Coach doesn't block, Tinker deals 2 damage to face. Either outcome is favorable.",
      "action_taken": "Did not attack with Watertrap Weaver.",
      "better_line": "Attack with Watertrap Weaver. If blocked by Celestial Enforcer, cast Chilling Trap on the Enforcer to save the Weaver, cantrip, and damage the Enforcer. If unblocked, deal 2 damage to Coach.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 67,
      "player": "Gem3F Tinker",
      "decision_index": 46,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Declined to block Celestial Enforcer (2/3) with Littjara Kinseekers (2/4) when blocking was completely safe. Both creatures survive combat (2 damage each, neither dies), opponent has no mana open for combat tricks, and blocking prevents 2 unnecessary damage.",
      "action_taken": "Did not block, taking 2 damage to go to 18 life.",
      "better_line": "Block Celestial Enforcer with Littjara Kinseekers. Both creatures survive, 2 damage is prevented, and there is zero risk since opponent has no mana available.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 87,
      "player": "Gem3F Tinker",
      "decision_index": 61,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Declined to cast Chilling Trap for {U} when controlling a Wizard (Watertrap Weaver), which would cantrip (draw a card) in addition to the -4/-0 effect. With 2 untapped Islands and nothing else to spend mana on, this is a 1-mana cantrip that could dig toward lands or better cards. The -4/-0 is relatively unimportant since opponent's creatures are tapped/sick, but the card draw is pure value.",
      "action_taken": "Passed on casting Chilling Trap, saving it for later.",
      "better_line": "Cast Chilling Trap targeting any of the opponent's creatures (e.g., Brightmare or Celestial Enforcer) to draw a card for {U}, using spare mana to dig deeper into the library while still having 1 Island untapped.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 100,
      "player": "Gem3F Tinker",
      "decision_index": 68,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Declined to cast Chilling Trap when controlling a Wizard (Watertrap Weaver), which would have drawn a card for just {U}. The -4/-0 could target the already-tapped Celestial Enforcer or the summoning-sick Brightmare with no downside, effectively making this a 1-mana cantrip. The opponent has no untapped blockers, so saving Chilling Trap as a combat trick has little value compared to the card advantage.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without casting Chilling Trap",
      "better_line": "Cast Chilling Trap targeting Celestial Enforcer or Brightmare to draw a card for {U}, then proceed to attacks with the extra card in hand.",
      "type": "blunder",
